Boundary data
-------------

Boundary data from geoBoundaries (www.geoboundaries.org), CC BY 4.0.

Nomos resolves Locations against the geoBoundaries Comprehensive Global Administrative Zones
(CGAZ) ADM0 and ADM1 layers, release v6.0.0, commit 1289e40e366c7b320550be1ee0614a9472d572d4 of
https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries. The data is not included in this repository or in the
Nomos package; `nomos build-index` downloads it into the user's cache. Nomos uses it unmodified,
apart from building a local lookup index from it.

geoBoundaries is built by the community and the William & Mary geoLab, and is released under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Citation:
  Runfola, D. et al. (2020) geoBoundaries: A global database of political administrative
  boundaries. PLoS ONE 15(4): e0231866. https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0231866

Region and Country names, Region IDs and boundaries come from geoBoundaries. Disputed areas in
CGAZ follow US Department of State definitions. Locations are for display and are not
determinations of sovereignty.

The fixture Dataset release in tests/fixtures/dataset/ is hand-drawn for testing and is not
derived from geoBoundaries data.
